<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Metway half year net profit A$34 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Metway half year net profit A$34 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to December 31</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     74 vs 33</p>
<p>    Net profit			     34 vs 13</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     18 vs 11</p>
<p>NOTE: Metway Bank Ltd is a Queensland-based regional bank which merged in November 1996 with the Queensland government-owned Suncorp Insurance Finance and Queensland Industry Development Corp.  </p>
<p>    Bad and doubtful debts		  2 vs   3</p>
<p>    Interest income			 394 vs 321</p>
<p>    Interest expense			271 vs 226</p>
<p>    Other income			     27 vs  18</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   14.99 vs 7.14</p>
<p>    Abnormal items (net)	    loss 16 vs loss 9</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date April 1</p>
<p>Reg date March 21</p>
<p>    Tax					  23 vs 14</p>
<p>NOTE: Metway said the abnormal loss reflected the write off of software development costs in relation to projects discontinued during the half.  </p>
<p>NOTE: Operating profit by business activity</p>
<p>    Banking				    49 vs 33</p>
<p>    General insurance			23 vs nil</p>
<p>    Life insurance			    1 vs nil</p>
<p>    Other activities			  1 vs nil</p>
<p>    Total assets			  18.43 vs 6.81</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
